<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

A prominent, in-page message that draws attention to a status or event.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/alert)

<%= embed UI::AlertPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Alert(variant: :info) do
  AlertIcon { info_icon }
  AlertTitle { "Scheduled maintenance" }
  AlertDescription { "Some features may be unavailable Sunday night." }
end
```

Alert is a banner for a message that lives in the page layout - a status, a heads-up, a result. Compose it
from its parts:

- `Alert` - the `role="alert"` container. Sets the variant color and layout, and owns the optional dismiss behavior.
- `AlertIcon` - a leading icon slot that automatically takes the variant's color.
- `AlertTitle` - the headline (`<h5>`).
- `AlertDescription` - the supporting body text.
- `AlertAction` - a trailing row for buttons.

The slots are placed by a grid, so include only the ones you need. For a transient, stacked notification
use a [Toast](<%= page_path(:toast) %>) instead; for a blocking confirmation, a dialog.

## Examples

### Variants

Seven variants color the alert for its purpose: `:default`, `:primary`, `:secondary`, `:info`, `:success`,
`:warning` and `:error`. The `AlertIcon` inherits the variant's accent color.

<%= embed UI::AlertPreview, :variants %>

### Inline layout

`layout: :inline` flows the icon, title and description onto a single row once there's room. The alert is a
container-query box, so it falls back to the stacked layout when it gets narrow - good for slim page-top banners.

<%= embed UI::AlertPreview, :inline %>

### With actions

Add an `AlertAction` row for buttons. It sits below the text in the block layout and trails the message inline.

<%= embed UI::AlertPreview, :actions %>

### Dismissible

`dismissible: true` adds a close button; the alert scales down, blurs and collapses away. To remember the
dismissal across visits give it a `persist_key:` - the choice is stored in `localStorage` (or
`sessionStorage` with `persist_storage: :session`) and the alert stays hidden on return.

<%= embed UI::AlertPreview, :dismissible %>

```ruby
Alert(variant: :primary, dismissible: true, persist_key: "reports-announcement") { … }
```

### Controlled

The Stimulus controller sits on the alert's outer box. Set its `data-ui--alert-open-value` to `"true"` /
`"false"` to show or hide it (animated), and listen for `ui--alert:open-change` (`{ open }`) - here to bring
a dismissed alert back. `open: false` renders the alert closed.

<%= embed UI::AlertPreview, :controlled %>

```js
box.addEventListener("ui--alert:open-change", ({ detail }) => showButton.hidden = detail.open)
showButton.addEventListener("click", () => box.setAttribute("data-ui--alert-open-value", "true"))
```

### RTL

The icon moves to the right, the dismiss button to the left, and the action row aligns to the start edge -
all from CSS logical properties.

<%= embed UI::AlertPreview, :rtl %>

## API reference

### Alert

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `variant:` | `:default`, `:primary`, `:secondary`, `:info`, `:success`, `:warning`, `:error` | `:default` | Color scheme; also drives the `AlertIcon` accent. |
| `layout:` | `:block`, `:inline` | `:block` | Stack the parts, or flow them on one row when wide enough. |
| `dismissible:` | `Boolean` | `false` | Render a close button that hides the alert (with an exit animation). |
| `open:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Initial visibility; drive it later through `data-ui--alert-open-value`. |
| `persist_key:` | `String` | - | Remember the dismissal under this key so the alert stays hidden on return. |
| `persist_storage:` | `:local`, `:session` | `:local` | Which Web Storage backs `persist_key:`. |
| `close_label:` | `String` | `"Dismiss"` | Accessible label for the close button. |
| `role:` | `String` | `"alert"` | Live-region role. Use `"status"` for a polite, non-interruptive alert. |

Other attributes (`class:`, `id:`, `data:` …) go to the `role="alert"` element; `class:` is merged with tailwind_merge.

Actions: `ui--alert#dismiss`, `ui--alert#show`. Event: `ui--alert:open-change` with `{ open }`.

### AlertIcon, AlertDescription, AlertAction

Render a `<span>`, `<p>` and `<div>`; they take any attributes, and `class:` is merged.

### AlertTitle

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `as:` | `:h1` … `:h6`, `:div` | `:h5` | Heading level, so the alert fits the page's outline. |

## Accessibility

- Alert renders with `role="alert"`, so assistive tech announces its contents when it appears - keep the
  message concise. It's an assertive live region: mount it when there's something to announce, or use
  `role: "status"` for a polite one.
- The dismiss button is a real `<button>` named by `close_label:`; customize it when "Dismiss" is ambiguous.
- `AlertIcon` is decorative - convey meaning in the title and description, not the icon alone.
- The exit/enter animation is skipped when the user prefers reduced motion. With `persist_key:` the alert
  is hidden when the controller connects, so a remembered alert can flash briefly on a full page load -
  prefer rendering it with `open: false` when the server knows it was dismissed.
